.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt OPEN 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm open
.Nd open files, folders and applications
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl e | Fl t | Fl a Ar application | Fl b Ar bundle-id
.Op Fl R
.Op Fl n
.Ar file ...
.Op Fl -args Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens each
.Ar file
with the application that opens its kind of file, as a double click in the
file manager does: folders open in it, applications are launched, documents go
to their application (launched if it is not running).
The choice is made by LaunchServices from the document types the
installed applications declare.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-b bundle-id"
.It Fl a Ar application
Open with this application, given by name (looked up in
.Pa /Applications ,
.Pa /System/Applications
and
.Pa /System/Library/CoreServices )
or by path.
With no files, the application is launched or brought to the front.
.It Fl b Ar bundle-id
Open with the application with this bundle identifier.
.It Fl e , Fl t
Open with Text Editor, the text editor.
.It Fl R , Fl -reveal
Show the files in the file manager, each selected in a window on its folder,
instead of opening them.
.It Fl n
Start a new instance of the application even if one is running.
.It Fl -args Ar argument ...
Give the remaining arguments to the application as its own, after the
path of its executable.
They reach it only when
.Nm
launches it: an application already running gets none.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr launchctl 1
